.TH ANIM 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
Anim \- One named animation: a contiguous run of frames on a sheet and how fast to play them
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqsprite.h\(dq
.ft B
typedef struct Anim   { int first, count; float frame_time; bool loop; } Anim;
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
One named animation: a contiguous run of frames on a sheet and how fast to play them. Define them as static const data, one per action, usually in an array indexed by an enum: static const Anim cat_anims[] = { [CAT_IDLE] = { 0, 4, 0.25f, true }, [CAT_RUN] = { 4, 6, 0.08f, true } };. An Anim holds no playback position; that is AnimState.
.SH FIELDS
.TP
.B first
sheet index of the first frame
.TP
.B count
number of frames; 1 is a still
.TP
.B frame_time
seconds each frame is shown
.TP
.B loop
true to wrap around forever, false to stop on the last frame and set AnimState.done
.SH MODULE
sprite (src/engine/sprite/sprite.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR AnimState (3),
.BR anim_step (3),
.BR anim_frame (3),
